-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",108,{
[3425]="70068414\n1\tCollect crab claws ([see journal]/12)\tHead south and east along the river shore and hunt the crabs there for their claws.\n2\tCollect crab claws ([see journal]/12)\tAfter collecting several claws to meet Tevurin's quota you need to return them to him at the hunter's expedition encampment in southeastern Cape of Umbar.\n",
[3426]="700454FB\n1\tDefeat Firien láthbears (total: 10)\tLáthbears can be found around the Firien Wood in the Beacon Hills. You should defeat láthbears.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many láthbears in the Beacon Hills.\n",
[3427]="7005AAAB\n1\tDefeat cave-claws and deep-claws in the Pit of Stonejaws (total: 12)\tTunnels in the north-east side of the Pit of Stonejaws contain many cave-claws and deep-claws.\n2\tTalk to Gráfar Splitstone\tGráfar Splitstone waits to hear about your efforts against the cave-claws.\n",
[3428]="7001548B\n1\tDefeat deep-claws (total: 12)\tDeep-claws can be found in the Great Delving, especially on the east path from the Dolven-view. You should defeat many deep-claws in the Great Delving, but it would be wise to focus your attention on the east path towards Zelem-melek.\n2\tReturn to Wafri in the Dolven-view\tWafri is in the Dolven-view camp in the Great Delving. You should speak with Wafri and tell him that you've defeated many deep-claws in the surrounding area.\n",
[3429]="7000838C\n1\tBring the blade-beak ravager beaks to Reko at Lehmä-koti.\030Collect blade-beak ravager beaks (total: 10)\tBlade-beak ravagers can be found throughout Ram Dúath. Reko has asked you to collect the blade-beak ravager beaks he desires.\n",
[3430]="7004CE4A\n1\tClean up mud in the barracks (total: 10)\tMud can be found in the guards' barracks in Lake-town. You should clean up mud.\n2\tTalk to Álarr\tCaptain Álarr can be found in the guards' barracks in Lake-town. You should talk to Álarr.\n",
[3431]="7000EC03\n1\tDefeat Coldfells soldiers (total: 10)\tThe Free Peoples' guards can be found at their encampments throughout the Ettenmoors, mostly to the south-east. Forzunk instructed you to defeat the Free Peoples' guards.\n2\tTalk to Forzunk at Gramsfoot\tForzunk is at Gramsfoot. You should tell Forzunk of your victories against the soldiers of the Coldfells.\n",
[3432]="7005B1F2\n1\tBurn spider corpses at Dalugronk\tBurning the spider corpses at Dalugronk would mean less food for the bats, and more time dedicated to hunting again.\n2\tBurn spider corpses (total: 5)\tBurning the spider corpses at Dalugronk would mean less food for the bats, and more time dedicated to hunting again.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have burned all the spider corpses at Dalugronk, depriving the bats of their food.\n",
[3433]="7004A8F3\n1\tBurn slain Orcs from Shagrat's garrison in Cirith Ungol (total: 12)\tSlain Orcs from Shagrat's garrison can be found throughout Cirith Ungol. Disappointed in the actions of his predecessor, Captain Róglarg has asked you to burn any slain Orcs you discover in Cirith Ungol.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have burned many of the dead Orcs from Shagrat's garrison.\n",
[3434]="7005A677\n1\tDestroy intact stone trolls (total: 6)\030Destroy broken stone trolls (total: 10)\tStone trolls can be found west of Maergrind. You should destroy any of the stone trolls that you find.\n2\tTalk to Grámi Hornhelm\tGrámi Hornhelm can be found at Maergrind in Máttugard. You should talk to Grámi Hornhelm.\n",
[3435]="70068BDF\n1\tFind the hidden store-room\tMânobaz has asked you to steal a portion of spoils that is rightfully his from the The Eastern Stores. The Eastern Stores can be found on the east side of the Lower Ward in the Cistern.\n2\tCollect Mânobaz's plunder (total: 8)\tYou have found the Eastern Stores. The plunder should be stored within.\n3\tTalk to Mânobaz\tYou have collected a good amount of spoils. Perhaps this is enough for Mânobaz. Mânobaz can be found next to the Black Anchor.\n",
[3436]="70071612\n1\tDefeat Ordâkhai in Emax Dûl (total: 15)\030Defeat Onadrókha Bóro\030Defeat Istoráli Bóro\030Defeat Sondrókor Bóro\tMany Ordâkhai still fight in the streets for control of Emax Dûl. You should defeat the Ordâkhai and their remaining captains: Onadrókha Bóro, Istoráli Bóro, and Sondrókor Bóro.\n2\tTalk to Numûru\tYou have done much to defeat the Ordâkhai in Emax Dûl. You should return to Numûru in Nashûbu.\n",
[3437]="7001BEB4\n1\tDefeat snow-troll bruisers (total: 8)\030Defeat snow-troll hurlers (total: 8)\tSnow-trolls can be found deep within Sarnúr, south of Thorin's Hall reached through the ruins of Orodost. Snár has asked you to enter the ancient ruins of Sarnúr and defeat a number of the snow-trolls gathered there.\n2\tTalk to Snár in Thorin's Hall\tSnár is in Thorin's Hall, north of Sarnúr, just outside the Blue Stone Garrison. You should return to Snár with news of your victory against the snow-trolls.\n",
[3438]="7004186D\n1\tTalk to Tucharn\tTucharn can be found in Erynos in eastern Lebennin. Glathril is unclear how the Corsairs met with such a fate and asks you to speak to Tucharn.\n2\tCorsairs can be found along the road outside Erynos. Tucharn has asked you to look over the fallen Corsairs on the road out of Erynos.\t\n3\tTalk to Glathril\tGlathril can be found in Erynos in eastern Lebennin. You have examined the fallen Corsairs and should now return to Glathril.\n4\tTalk to Nimithil in Ost Anglebed\tNimithil can be found in Ost Anglebed in north-central Lebennin. You have found the people of Erynos safe from harm, and should now tell Nimithil of what happened.\n",
[3439]="700032A6\n1\tCollect damp fragrant herbs (total: 3)\tThe herbs can be found along the riverside beneath Duillond. Calengil has asked you to retrieve the herbs that he needs to complete the cleansing draught.\n2\tReturn the herbs you collected to Calengil\tCalengil is at Duillond, north of Celondim. You should return the herbs you collected to Calengil.\n",
[3440]="70050E14\n1\tDefeat Ungoledain (total: 8)\tYou should defeat Ungoledain in the old ruins at Kêr Bréin.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many Ungoledain in the old ruins at Kêr Bréin.\n",
[3441]="700304B8\n1\tBurn the large tents in Jóshkhin Orda\tLarge tents can be found throughout the large encampment of Jóshkhin Orda to the north of North-torr. Torches can be found near some camp-fires throughout the camp. You should collect a torch from the camp-fire and use it to light the doorway of the large Easterling tent.\n2\tFind a torch and burn the large Easterling tent\tLarge tents can be found throughout the large encampment of Jóshkhin Orda to the north of North-torr. Torches can be found near some camp-fires throughout the camp. You should collect a torch from the camp-fire and use it to light the doorway of the large Easterling tent.\n3\tBurn the small Easterling tents to the south-west\tA pair of small tents lie to the south-west of the largest tent in Jóshkhin Orda. You should collect a torch from a nearby camp-fire and set the tents ablaze.\n4\tBurn the small Easterling tents to the south-east\tA pair of small tents lie to the south-east of the largest tent in Jóshkhin Orda. You should collect a torch from a nearby camp-fire and set the tents ablaze.\n5\tReturn to Guthferth, Sergeant of North-torr\tSergeant Guthferth is rallying the defences of North-torr just north of Floodwend, attempting to hold back the flood of Easterlings threatening to drown the Wold in chaos. You should return to Sergeant Guthferth with news of your success.\n",
[3442]="7003A620\n1\tDefeat the Boar-tribe Orcs\tWhile you are in the Boar-tribe lair, you should defeat as many of the Orcs as possible.\n2\tDefeat the Boar-tribe Orcs (total: 10)\tWhile you are in the Boar-tribe lair, you should defeat as many of the Orcs as possible.\n3\tCompleted\tMany Boar-tribe Orcs were defeated as you made your way through their cave.\n",
[3443]="700588FF\n1\tBurn piles of Orc-filth (total: 8)\tPiles of Orc-filth can be found along river-beds in Elderslade. Mother Amma has tasked you with cleansing the rivers that flow into the Dvergvát.\n2\tTalk to Mother Amma\tMother Amma is in Annâk-khurfu, in eastern Elderslade. You should talk to Mother Amma.\n",
[3444]="70009E7A\n1\tCleanse the Hoarwell River of the poison introduced by Angmar\tThe poison was introduced to the Hoarwell at the waterfall overlooking Tol Ascarnen, in the central area of the Ettenmoors, north-west of Glán Vraig. Captain-General Tordúr asked you to make your way to the top of the waterfall overlooking Tol Ascarnen to assist in cleansing the poison that the goblins of Angmar introduced into the Hoarwell River.\n2\tTalk to Captain-General Tordúr\tCaptain-General Tordúr is at Glân Vraig. You should return to Captain-General Tordúr with news of your success.\n",
[3445]="7004DA3B\n1\tCollect phials (total: 10)\tYou should collect phials of the Elves' healing draught from within Felegoth.\n2\tDefeat corrupted roots (total: 10)\030Sprinkle trees in need with the healing draught (quantity: see journal)\tYou should defeat corrupted roots and give water to trees in need throughout Eryn Lasgalen.\n3\tTalk to Radagast\tYou should return to Radagast, who can be found at the tree nursery just outside of Felegoth.\n",
[3446]="70070CCA\n1\tCleanse corrupted trees (total: 6)\030Defeat Huorns in Hordírid (total: 6)\tYour mission is to travel to Hordírid to the north-west to stop the dangerous Huorns and to cleanse the corrupted trees in the area.\n2\tDefeat the vicious Adagím Huorn\tYour mission is to travel to Hordírid to the north-west to stop the dangerous Huorns and to cleanse the corrupted trees in the area.\n",
[3447]="7000329E\n1\tUse the draught near the first tower\030Find the first tower of Dol Ringwest\030Use the draught near the second tower\030Find the second tower of Dol Ringwest\tDol Ringwest is west of Duillond. Calengil bade you pour the cleansing draught upon the ground at the base of two towers that remain standing in the ruins of Dol Ringwest.\n2\tReturn to Calengil in Duillond, east of Dol Ringwest\tCalengil is in Duillond, east of Dol Ringwest. You should return to Calengil and inform him that your task in the ruins of Dol Ringwest is complete.\n",
[3448]="70030444\n1\tDefeat Wargs in The Howling Wood (total: 8)\tWargs can be found at the abandoned worksite east of Floodwend. You should defeat many Wargs in the forest to the east.\n2\tTell Thane Radwig of your victory against the Wargs\tThe young Thane Radwig can be found in the Mead Hall of Floodwend. You should return to the Thane.\n",
[3449]="70014879\n1\tClear rubble (total: 8)\tThe rock-fall that Sót has asked you to clear can be found in the eastern side of the Great Delving, south of the gate leading to the Lonely Span. Sót, the librarian of the Dolven-view expedition, has asked you to aid him by clearing the road leading to the Lonely Span of debris and rubble.\n2\tTalk to Sót at the Dolven-view camp\tSót is at the Dolven-view camp, south-west of the Lonely Span. The rubble from the rock-fall has been cleared out. You should return to Sót and let him know.\n",
[3450]="70007B4C\n1\tFill the water-bladder\030Fill the water-bladder at the Last Bridge\tThe Last Bridge lies at the eastern end of the Great East Road. Northrim gave you an empty, cured bladder and asked you to collect water from the Hoarwell on the northern side of the Last Bridge.\n2\tBring the full water-bladder to Northrim\tNorthrim awaits your return with clean water at Dol Vaeg, west of the Last Bridge. You made your way to the Hoarwell's edge and collected water from the banks. You should return at once to Northrim.\n",
[3451]="70054656\n1\tDefeat Orcs to the east of Barad Angarth (total: 10)\tThe Orcs that threaten the Rangers can be found to the east of Barad Angarth. Deplete the Orc forces as you make your way further into the encampment.\n2\tTalk to Dorgam within the Orc encampment\tInform Dorgam that you have defeated some of the forces surrounding his position. He is east of Barad Angarth.\n",
[3452]="70007F71\n1\tDefeat bears in the Vale of Thráin (total: 8)\tHunter's Notch can be found north of Noglond. Ketill has asked you to hunt bears in Hunter's Notch and cull their numbers.\n2\tTalk to Ketill\tKetill is in Noglond, south of Thorin's Hall. You should return to Ketill and report the results of your patrol.\n",
[3453]="700037FE\n1\tDefeat Blue-crag Spoiler (total: 3)\030Defeat Blue-crag Novice (total: 3)\030Defeat Blue-crag Trapper\tThe canal near Gondamon is to the west, past the hills. Otkell, the Chief Builder of Gondamon, informed you that goblins are responsible for the lack of fresh water. He asked you to go to the area west of the canal and remove the goblin threat.\n2\tTalk to Otkell\tOtkell is at Gondamon to the east of the canal, beyond the hills. You should return to Otkell and tell him about the goblins you defeated.\n",
[3454]="700272BC\n1\tDefeat Orcs at Ak-ghru (total: 10)\tOrcs can be found at Ak-ghru. Elfrith has asked you to defeat many of the clear-cutting Orcs.\n2\tTalk to Elfrith\tElfrith is hiding beyond the bounds of Ak-ghru. You should return to Elfrith with news of your success.\n",
[3455]="7004A906\n1\tDestroy broodling eggs (total: 5)\030Burn encroaching webs (total: 10)\tBroodling eggs and encroaching webs can be found in Cirith Ungol's courtyard and the tower interior. You should destroy broodling eggs and encroaching webs.\n",
[3456]="70058672\n1\tDefeat hobgoblins in Malkorlash (total: 12)\tMalkorlash is in northern Elderslade. You should defeat enemies at the hobgoblin camp, Malkorlash.\n2\tTalk to Borghild\tBorghild is north-east of Malkorlash in eastern Elderslade. Talk to Borghild.\n",
})
